Android-native mergers (documented in SURVEY.md):
  PrintButton/FullscreenButton/PinButton  -> controlled Compose primitives (host owns browser/Fleet API,
    out of scope per prompt). TeslaGlyphs.kt -> native stroked ImageVectors (lucide-react has no Android peer).
  ThemePicker/ThemeController -> mode + high-contrast + Material You (web accent/custom-color N/A; brand = single M3 scheme).

Out of scope (documented in SURVEY.md): CommandPalette (app-shell), SignalConfigModal (domain feature),
  PlaybackControls (data-display re-export), *.test.tsx (re-covered by Kotlin tests below).

================================================================================
STEP 2-5 — IMPLEMENTATION
================================================================================
  47 component/foundation .kt files under app/src/main/java/io/teslasync/android/components/ui/ (~4,000 LOC).
  Foundation: TeslaGlyphs.kt, Density.kt, Typography.kt, ThemeController.kt, UiLogic.kt.
  All states implemented: loading (Button/ConfirmDialog/CopyButton), disabled (every control),
  error (Input/Textarea/Select/EditableText), empty (DataTable emptyText / MaskedValue em-dash).
  a11y: contentDescription on every actionable icon; Role.Checkbox/Switch/Button via toggleable/clickable;
  TriStateCheckbox; paneTitle on dialogs; FormLabel required announcement; 48dp targets via Material
  IconButton / minimumInteractiveComponentSize.
  Tokens: only MaterialTheme.{colorScheme,typography,shapes} + generated Spacing/Radius/Elevation +
  TeslaTokens.{status,chart}. No raw hex / web CSS values in component code.
  Previews: ComponentGallery.kt -> @Preview Light / Dark / High-contrast galleries.

